(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// sys.monitoring's call-family events (PEP 669; queue 220, Python/instrumentation.c and Python/legacy_tracing.c of"] [4 1 "// CPython 3.14.10, PSF License Agreement): the tools' registry (use_tool_id, free_tool_id, clear_tool_id, get_tool),"] [5 1 "// their global events (set_events, get_events) and callbacks (register_callback), and the events a profiler needs:"] [6 1 "// PY_START, PY_RESUME, PY_THROW, PY_RETURN, PY_YIELD, PY_UNWIND at a frame's start and end (runFrames), CALL, C_RETURN"] [7 1 "// and C_RAISE at the call sites of the loop and of compiled code (eval.go, aot.go). sys.setprofile is the legacy tool"] [8 1 "// over them (PY_MONITORING_SYS_PROFILE_ID 6), as legacy_tracing.c makes it. _lsprof (builtins_lsprof.go) is a tool."] [9 1 "//"] [10 1 "// Off, an event costs one load of monEvents (0 when no tool has an event) and a branch. A callback runs with the thread's"] [11 1 "// tracing count up (tstate->tracing): no event fires inside it. Not built: the local events (set_local_events,"] [12 1 "// get_local_events record nothing), LINE, INSTRUCTION, JUMP, BRANCH*, RAISE, RERAISE, EXCEPTION_HANDLED and"] [13 1 "// STOP_ITERATION never fire (settrace's are 219's), DISABLE returned by a callback disables nothing, restart_events is a"] [14 1 "// no-op. CALL's instruction_offset is 2 x the IR's instruction (f_lasti's unit)."] [16 1 "// the events' numbers (the bit index of sys.monitoring.events' values)"] [28 2 "// monProfileTool is the legacy profiler's tool (PY_MONITORING_SYS_PROFILE_ID)"] [33 1 "// monCallFamily are the events a profiler uses (legacy_tracing.c's for sys.setprofile)"] [37 1 "// monTool is a tool's registration: its name (nil: free), its global events, its callbacks by event."] [42 2 "// native, for the legacy profiler: called in place of cb"] [48 2 "// monEvents is the union of every tool's global events: the hooks' one load"] [50 2 "// monMissing and monDisable are sys.monitoring.MISSING and DISABLE"] [53 2 "// monTracing are the threads running a callback (tstate->tracing); under the GIL"] [57 1 "// monUpdate recomputes monEvents, and breakMonitor in the eval breaker: a frame's start checks the breaker alone, so"] [58 1 "// its PY_START costs nothing while no tool has an event."] [72 1 "// monFire calls the tools' callbacks of event ev with args; the first error is returned (raised where the event is)."] [108 1 "// monEnter is a frame's start in runFrames: PY_THROW for an exception thrown into a generator's frame, PY_START for a"] [109 1 "// frame at its first instruction, else PY_RESUME."] [128 1 "// monLeave is a frame's return of v in runFrames: PY_YIELD when it is suspended, else PY_RETURN."] [140 1 "// monUnwind is a frame left by exc (PY_UNWIND); a callback's error replaces the exception."] [153 1 "// monCall is CALL before a call of callable from f, arg0 its first argument (self for a method) or nil."] [164 1 "// monCReturn is C_RETURN or C_RAISE after a call of callable, not a Python function, from f: the call's result, or a"] [165 1 "// callback's error."] [183 1 "// monCallC is a call of a callable that is not a Python function from f with monitoring on: CALL, the call, then"] [184 1 "// C_RETURN or C_RAISE."] [197 1 "// isPyFunction is whether a call of o runs a Python frame (a function, or a bound method of one): no C events."] [210 1 "// the legacy profiler (sys.setprofile): each thread's function, and how many threads have one"] [225 1 "// setProfile is _PyEval_SetProfile for t: fn None removes it."] [235 1 "// profileCFunc is the C function a CALL's callable stands for (legacy_tracing.c's sys_profile_call_or_return): a"] [236 1 "// built-in function or method itself, a method descriptor bound to its first argument; nil for any other callable."] [250 1 "// builtinOwner is the type in arg0's type's MRO whose dict holds b (a method descriptor's d_type), or nil."] [263 1 "// profileEvent is the legacy tool's callback: the thread's profile function called as (frame, event, arg); an error"] [264 1 "// removes it (sys.setprofile(None)) and is raised."] [298 1 "// newMonitoringModule is sys.monitoring."] [453 1 "// monCallSite is a call site's monitoring (queue 220): CALL fired; a callable that is no Python function called here"] [454 1 "// with C_RETURN or C_RAISE after it (done true, its result); a Python function's call left to the site (done false)."] [471 1 "// callStackMon is callStack's monitoring: monCallSite over the call's callable and arguments on f's stack, which a C"] [472 1 "// callable's call pops."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[83 41] [94 21] [145 79] [146 29] [177 78] [190 40] [199 27] [203 36] [243 36] [257 25] [289 20] [346 29] [383 28] [400 22] [427 13] [427 29] [460 40] [480 40]]} (go/file "monitoring.go" :imports [])

;; sys.monitoring's call-family events (PEP 669; queue 220, Python/instrumentation.c and Python/legacy_tracing.c of
;; CPython 3.14.10, PSF License Agreement): the tools' registry (use_tool_id, free_tool_id, clear_tool_id, get_tool),
;; their global events (set_events, get_events) and callbacks (register_callback), and the events a profiler needs:
;; PY_START, PY_RESUME, PY_THROW, PY_RETURN, PY_YIELD, PY_UNWIND at a frame's start and end (runFrames), CALL, C_RETURN
;; and C_RAISE at the call sites of the loop and of compiled code (eval.go, aot.go). sys.setprofile is the legacy tool
;; over them (PY_MONITORING_SYS_PROFILE_ID 6), as legacy_tracing.c makes it. _lsprof (builtins_lsprof.go) is a tool.
;;
;; Off, an event costs one load of monEvents (0 when no tool has an event) and a branch. A callback runs with the thread's
;; tracing count up (tstate->tracing): no event fires inside it. Not built: the local events (set_local_events,
;; get_local_events record nothing), LINE, INSTRUCTION, JUMP, BRANCH*, RAISE, RERAISE, EXCEPTION_HANDLED and
;; STOP_ITERATION never fire (settrace's are 219's), DISABLE returned by a callback disables nothing, restart_events is a
;; no-op. CALL's instruction_offset is 2 x the IR's instruction (f_lasti's unit).


